# IRR server configuration — local single-user personal application ONLY.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in the IPD values for this machine, then start the API
# with `npm run server:dev` (which loads `.env.local` if it exists) and the UI with `npm run dev`.
#
# These settings are read SERVER-SIDE ONLY, from the API process environment. Nothing here is ever
# accepted from an HTTP request, a header, a cookie or a query string, and no value on this page is
# an owner, tenant, principal or credential. They are local startup preconditions, not authority:
# IPD still resolves the active owner binding and still enforces its own write guards per request.
#
# Without these, `/api/user-portfolios*` fails closed with `503`, and the UI now says which setting
# is missing instead of reporting an empty portfolio. That refusal is correct, not a defect.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for any durable user-portfolio READ (list, detail, revisions).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IRR-local precondition: an operator has provisioned an IPD A-2 local binding.
# Fail-closed default: anything other than true/1/yes is treated as absent.
IIPS_G3_IPC_BINDING_PROVISIONED=true

# The same-host IPC target IPD listens on. A local socket path or endpoint name — NEVER a URL
# or a host:port (both are refused). POSIX example:
#   IIPS_G2_IPC_ENDPOINT=/run/iips/user-portfolio.sock
# Windows named pipe example (operator runbook §3.1):
#   IIPS_G2_IPC_ENDPOINT=\\.\pipe\iips-user-portfolio-v1
# A bare name (letters, digits, dot, underscore, hyphen) is resolved against
# IIPS_G2_IPC_STATE_DIR, which must then be an absolute directory.
# IIPS_G2_IPC_ENDPOINT=/run/iips/user-portfolio.sock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Additional enablement required for CREATE / SAVE / DELETE. A condition, never authority.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# When absent or not exactly `1`, every write route answers
# `503 {"error":"operation-not-admitted"}` before a port is constructed or a body is read.
# IPD's own W-1 default-deny remains in force upstream of this switch either way.
# IIPS_LOCAL_PERSONAL_USE=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unrelated owner-scoped surfaces. Do NOT alias one carrier to another; each needs its own file.
# See docs/OPERATOR_RUNBOOK.md. Left unset these surfaces simply stay unavailable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IIPS_OWNER_CONTEXT_PATH=/abs/path/owner-context.json
# IIPS_REPORTS_OWNER_PATH=/abs/path/reports-owner-context.json
# IIPS_BROKER_EVIDENCE_OWNER_PATH=/abs/path/broker-evidence-owner-context.json
# IIPS_NP04_DATABASE_PATH=/abs/path/np04.sqlite
# IIPS_DATA_DIR=/abs/path/iips-data

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IPD market-data / identity transport. SERVER-SIDE ONLY — never prefix with VITE_,
# never place in frontend/.env, and never send to the browser. Read exclusively by
# server/market-data/marketDataTransportConfig.ts.
#
# Both are required together. While either is unset, the DHAN instrument search and
# identity routes (POST /api/dhan/instruments/search · /api/dhan/identity/resolve ·
# /api/dhan/identity/qualify) answer
#   503 {"error":{"code":"TRANSPORT_NOT_CONFIGURED","requiredSettings":[...]}}
# and no request is sent to IPD. That is a configuration state, not an IPD fault.
#
# The URL must be a loopback host (localhost / 127.0.0.1 / [::1]) over http: or https:,
# with no embedded credentials, query or fragment. The token is IPD's own transport
# bearer token; keep it out of shell history and version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IIPS_MARKET_DATA_TRANSPORT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8790
# IIPS_MARKET_DATA_TRANSPORT_TOKEN=
